/F1 7.5 Tf
8.625 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
201.5 535.1150000000000091 Td
(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (Under ICH guidelines and FDA 21 CFR 312.32, an adverse event is classified as Serious if it results in) Tj
T* (any of the following 6 seriousness criteria:) Tj
T* (1. Death of the patient.) Tj
T* (2. Life-threatening condition \(immediate risk of death at the time of the event\).) Tj
T* (3. Inpatient hospitalization or prolongation of existing hospitalization.) Tj
T* (4. Persistent or significant disability or incapacity.) Tj
T* (5. Congenital anomaly or birth defect in offspring.) Tj
T* (6. Other Medically Important Condition \(MIC\) that jeopardizes the patient and requires medical or surgical) Tj
T* (intervention to prevent one of the outcomes above \(e.g., intensive allergic bronchospasm, seizures not) Tj
T* (resulting in hospital admission\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Never forget the 6th criterion \('Medically Important Condition'\); forgetting MIC is the) Tj
T* (#1 mistake freshers make.) Tj
