(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (Expedited reporting timelines to health authorities \(US FDA, EMA, UK MHRA\) depend on outcome and) Tj
T* (expectedness:) Tj
T* (• 7-Calendar-Day Expedited Report: Mandatory for Serious, Unexpected, Suspected Adverse Reactions) Tj
T* (\(SUSARs\) that are Fatal or Life-Threatening. Initial submission must occur within 7 calendar days from) Tj
T* (Day 0, with a comprehensive follow-up report within an additional 8 calendar days \(Day 15\).) Tj
T* (• 15-Calendar-Day Expedited Report: Mandatory for all other Serious, Unexpected, Suspected Adverse) Tj
T* (Reactions \(SUSARs\) that are non-fatal and non-life-threatening \(e.g., hospitalization or permanent) Tj
T* (disability\).) Tj
T* (Non-serious cases are submitted in periodic reports \(PBRER/PSUR\) rather than expedited tracks.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Emphasize 'Calendar Days', not business/working days. Regulatory clocks do not) Tj
T* (stop on weekends or public holidays.) Tj
