201.5 280.2400000000000091 Td
(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (MedDRA \(Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities\) is the standardized international medical) Tj
T* (terminology developed by ICH for sharing regulatory data across pharmaceutical authorities.) Tj
T* (Its hierarchy comprises 5 distinct levels from broadest to most specific:) Tj
T* (1. System Organ Class \(SOC\) - 27 top-level physiological systems \(e.g., Cardiac disorders\).) Tj
T* (2. High-Level Group Term \(HLGT\) - Pathological or anatomical group \(e.g., Cardiac arrhythmias\).) Tj
T* (3. High-Level Term \(HLT\) - Specific group of conditions \(e.g., Ventricular arrhythmias and cardiac arrest\).) Tj
T* (4. Preferred Term \(PT\) - The definitive single medical concept used for aggregate data analysis \(e.g.,) Tj
T* (Ventricular tachycardia\).) Tj
T* (5. Lowest Level Term \(LLT\) - 80,000+ terms capturing exact verbatim reported terms including synonyms) Tj
T* (and colloquial expressions.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Clarify that in Oracle Argus, every reported adverse event verbatim is first matched) Tj
T* (to an LLT, which automatically assigns its linked PT and Primary SOC.) Tj
