(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (• Dechallenge: The withdrawal or discontinuation of the suspect drug from the patient. If the adverse) Tj
T* (reaction subsides or improves after stopping the medication, it is considered a 'Positive Dechallenge'. If) Tj
T* (symptoms continue or worsen, it is a 'Negative Dechallenge'.) Tj
T* (• Rechallenge: The intentional or accidental re-administration of the suspect drug after the event has) Tj
T* (resolved. If the adverse reaction recurs upon re-exposure, it is a 'Positive Rechallenge'—the strongest) Tj
T* (clinical evidence of drug causality. If the event does not recur, it is a 'Negative Rechallenge'.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Mention that in certain conditions \(like severe Stevens-Johnson syndrome or) Tj
T* (anaphylaxis\), re-challenging is medically unethical and contraindicated.) Tj
