(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (Causality assessment evaluates the likelihood that a medicinal product caused an observed adverse) Tj
T* (event. The two primary methods are:) Tj
T* (1. WHO-UMC Causality Categories: Categorizes cases into Certain, Probable/Likely, Possible, Unlikely,) Tj
T* (Conditional/Unclassified, and Unassessable/Unclassifiable based on time-to-onset, dechallenge,) Tj
T* (rechallenge, and plausible pharmacology.) Tj
T* (2. Naranjo Algorithm: A 10-question scoring questionnaire yielding scores from <=0 \(Doubtful\), 1-4) Tj
T* (\(Possible\), 5-8 \(Probable\), to >=9 \(Definite\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Highlight that in spontaneous post-marketing surveillance, if an HCP reports an AE,) Tj
T* (a default 'Possible' causality is assumed unless explicitly ruled out.) Tj
