(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (A Safety Signal is defined by WHO as reported information on a possible causal relationship between an) Tj
T* (adverse event and a drug, the relationship being unknown or incompletely documented previously.) Tj
T* (Quantitative Signal Detection uses statistical disproportionality algorithms comparing observed vs.) Tj
T* (expected event rates in vast safety databases \(like FDA FAERS or WHO VigiBase\):) Tj
T* (• PRR \(Proportional Reporting Ratio\): A PRR >= 2 with Chi-square >= 4 and at least 3 cases typically) Tj
T* (flags a signal.) Tj
T* (• ROR \(Reporting Odds Ratio\): Calculated using a 2x2 contingency table to measure the odds of an event) Tj
T* (occurring with the suspect drug versus all other drugs.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Clarify that a statistical signal is not proof of causality—it is a trigger for qualitative) Tj
T* (medical review and epidemiologic investigation.) Tj
