(MODEL ANSWER:) Tj
T* (ICH-GCP E6\(R2\) establishes ethical and quality standards for designing, conducting, recording, and) Tj
T* (reporting human clinical trials:) Tj
T* (1. Protection of Human Subjects: The rights, safety, and well-being of trial subjects prevail over the) Tj
T* (interests of science and society.) Tj
T* (2. Institutional Review Board / IEC Approval: Free and independent ethics committee sign-off prior to trial) Tj
T* (initiation.) Tj
T* (3. Freely Given Informed Consent: Mandatory written informed consent obtained from every subject) Tj
T* (before any study procedure.) Tj
T* (4. Qualified Investigators: Medical care governed exclusively by licensed, qualified physicians.) Tj
T* (5. Data Integrity & ALCOA++: All clinical trial records must be Attributable, Legible, Contemporaneous,) Tj
T* (Original, and Accurate.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Mention the 'ALCOA++' acronym when answering GCP questions—it signals) Tj
T* (immediate clinical trial maturity.) Tj
