T* (An RMP \(Risk Management Plan, EMA standard\) or REMS \(Risk Evaluation and Mitigation Strategy, US) Tj
T* (FDA standard\) is a dynamic regulatory document describing the safety profile of a medicinal product and) Tj
T* (actionable steps to prevent or minimize risks to patients.) Tj
T* (Three Key Components:) Tj
T* (1. Safety Specification: Identifies known risks \(important identified risks\), potential risks \(unproven) Tj
T* (associations\), and missing information \(e.g., use in pregnant women or severe renal patients\).) Tj
T* (2. Pharmacovigilance Plan: Outlines routine PV surveillance and additional post-authorization safety) Tj
T* (studies \(PASS\).) Tj
T* (3. Risk Minimization Measures: Special educational brochures, patient alert cards, controlled distribution,) Tj
T* (or physician checklist guides to mitigate serious reactions.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: Cite an example like Thalidomide \(mandatory pregnancy testing\) or Isotretinoin) Tj
T* (iPLEDGE program.) Tj
