T* ('Day 0' \(Clock Start\) is the exact calendar date on which any employee, contractual representative,) Tj
T* (vendor, or affiliate of the pharmaceutical marketing authorization holder \(MAH\) first becomes aware of a) Tj
T* (case containing all 4 minimum validity criteria.) Tj
T* (Crucial Rules:) Tj
T* (• Day 0 cannot be altered or reset when transferred between departments \(e.g., if a sales rep receives the) Tj
T* (report on Monday, Day 0 is Monday, even if PV receives it on Thursday\).) Tj
T* (• The 7-day or 15-day regulatory reporting clock begins counting from the calendar day following Day 0.) Tj
T* (• Clock start compliance is a primary metric evaluated during FDA and EMA regulatory inspections.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (INTERVIEWER TIP: State that late Day 0 receipt from commercial/field teams is the most common cause) Tj
T* (of regulatory inspection findings.) Tj
